    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-21T10:43:26+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T10:43:26+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T00:13:26Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T00:13:26Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak high pressure system about the west coast will move across the state today. A trough of low pressure and cold front move into the west late this evening and cross the remainder of of South Australia on Sunday. Another cold front clips the southeast on Monday, followed by a high pressure system, which will then move across southern parts of the state on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny day. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the evening. Winds north to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h increasing to 50 km/h before tending north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h in the late morning and early afternoon, then tending northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures around 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 13 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Woomera in the morning. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h before dawn then tending southerly 20 to 30 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to 20 to 28 with daytime temperatures reaching 32 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 32.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla in the evening. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
